+### 5.8 conversation_list
+
+The server answers an enabled `list_conversations` request with exactly one page of the authenticated user's summaries. The summary times are ISO strings, and this read is answered without a `stream_end`; when history is disabled or the store cannot list, the server answers with an `UNSUPPORTED` error instead ([validated by: accepts a paged list frame and delivers only the authenticated user’s newest ISO summaries](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L61), [validated by: returns UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+
+| Field           | Type                  | Description                                   |
+| --------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | string                | `"conversation_list"`                         |
+| `conversations` | ConversationSummary[] | Rows for the authenticated user, newest first |
+
+The user id comes from the authenticated connection and is never taken from the request frame. `transport.history` is opt-in; a disabled feature and a store without `listFor` both produce `UNSUPPORTED`, not an empty list ([validated by: accepts a paged list frame and delivers only the authenticated user’s newest ISO summaries](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L61), [validated by: returns UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled or the store cannot list](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
